│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that when playing Master System (SMS) games with      │
│ MiSTer-mapped controllers in the Mega Drive core, SMS buttons are  │
│ mapped as:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • SMS 1 -> Mega Drive A                                           │
│  • SMS 2 -> Mega Drive B                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ But expected behavior (and what happens with real/SNAC pads) is:   │
│                                                                    │
│  • SMS 1 -> Mega Drive B                                           │
│  • SMS 2 -> Mega Drive C                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in rtl/pad_io.sv, in the SMS branch of the pad output   │
│ mapping:                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  4'b1XXX: pdata <= { ~P_B, ~P_A, ~P_RIGHT, ~P_LEFT, ~P_DOWN,       │
│  ~P_UP};                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This SMS mapping uses P_A and P_B, which causes the observed A/B   │
│ behavior for MiSTer-mapped controllers.                            │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the change minimal and localized to SMS-specific mapping.  │
│  • Do not alter Mega Drive mode mappings (to avoid regressions in  │
│    normal Genesis/MD games).                                       │
│  • Match existing hardware/SNAC behavior for consistency.          │
│  • Preserve existing style and structure (single-line case         │
│    update).                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Update the SMS mapping in pad_io.sv to use B/C instead of A/B.     │
│ Concretely, replace {~P_B, ~P_A, ...} with {~P_C, ~P_B, ...} in    │
│ the SMS case.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This aligns MiSTer-mapped controllers with expected SMS behavior.  │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│ [file]rtl/pad_io.sv[/file] [original]always @(posedge clk) begin   │
│ priority casex({SMS,JCNT,TH}) 4'b1XXX: pdata <= { ~P_B,     ~P_A,  │
│ ~P_RIGHT, ~P_LEFT, ~P_DOWN, ~P_UP}; 4'b0100: pdata <= { ~P_START,  │
│ ~P_A,   1'b0,     1'b0,    1'b0,   1'b0}; 4'b0110: pdata <= {      │
