│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ For Master System mode, when using MiSTer-mapped controllers in    │
│ this core, SMS buttons are effectively mapped as:                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • SMS 1 → Mega Drive A                                            │
│  • SMS 2 → Mega Drive B                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ But expected/real hardware behavior (and SNAC behavior) is:        │
│                                                                    │
│  • SMS 1 → Mega Drive B                                            │
│  • SMS 2 → Mega Drive C                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ So the in-core digital pad mapping for SMS mode is off by one      │
│ button (shifted toward A/B instead of B/C).                        │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the bug is                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in rtl/pad_io.sv, in the gamepad output mux:          │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  4'b1XXX: pdata <= { ~P_B,     ~P_A, ~P_RIGHT, ~P_LEFT, ~P_DOWN,   │
│  ~P_UP};                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This is the SMS path (SMS=1) and currently uses P_B and P_A for    │
│ the two SMS buttons.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and localized to SMS mapping logic.        │
│  • Avoid changing global controller definitions or unrelated input │
│    modes.                                                          │
│  • Preserve existing MD/6-button/mouse/gun behavior.               │
│  • Match hardware/SNAC-consistent semantics (SMS uses MD B/C).     │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Change the SMS case in pad_io.sv to output P_C and P_B instead of  │
│ P_B and P_A for the two action bits.                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
