│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is a PMP/EPMP mismatch between Ibex and Spike for an     │
│ instruction fetch at a TOR boundary (0x80005cc4), specifically     │
│ when a 32-bit instruction straddles two PMP regions.               │
│ Spike correctly raises an instruction access fault on the second   │
│ half of the instruction; Ibex sometimes misses this.               │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the problem is                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv, in logic that decides when to  │
│ include the “+2” PMP check (pmp_err_if_plus2_i) for uncompressed   │
│ instructions.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Current code uses if_instr_addr[2] to detect unaligned 32-bit      │
│ instructions:                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • if_instr_pmp_err composition                                    │
│  • if_instr_err_plus2 bookkeeping                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ For RISC-V with 16-bit alignment, a 32-bit instruction is          │
│ “straddling” when it starts at address ...2 (i.e. addr[1] == 1),   │
│ not based on addr[2].                                              │
│ So the condition can incorrectly skip checking the second half of  │
│ the instruction.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Make the smallest possible RTL change to avoid unintended       │
│    behavior changes.                                               │
│  • Keep existing structure/signals intact; only fix the alignment  │
│    condition.                                                      │
│  • Preserve semantics for compressed instructions and bus error    │
│    handling.                                                       │
│  • Avoid changing PMP core policy logic unless necessary (not      │
│    needed here).                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ In ibex_if_stage.sv, replace if_instr_addr[2] with                 │
│ if_instr_addr[1] in the two places where second-half PMP error     │
│ handling is gated for uncompressed instructions.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ This correctly identifies halfword-misaligned 32-bit instructions  │
│ and ensures second-half PMP check is applied when needed.          │
