│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is a PMP execute-permission mismatch when a 32-bit       │
│ instruction starts at halfword offset +2 (straddling a 4-byte      │
│ boundary), and the second half lands in a different PMP TOR        │
│ region.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Spike correctly raises instruction access fault at the second half │
│ address (0x80005cc4), but Ibex sometimes does not.                 │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the bug is                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ The core already computes two instruction PMP checks (PMP_I at     │
│ pc_if, PMP_I2 at pc_if+2) in rtl/ibex_core.sv, which is correct.   │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug is in rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv where the IF stage decides      │
│ whether to consider the +2 error (pmp_err_if_plus2_i /             │
│ fetch_err_plus2).                                                  │
│ It currently uses if_instr_addr[2] as the “straddles boundary”     │
│ condition:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • if_instr_pmp_err logic                                          │
│  • if_instr_err_plus2 logic                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ For a 32-bit instruction at address ending in ...2, the relevant   │
│ bit is addr[1], not addr[2].                                       │
│ Using bit 2 suppresses the second-half check in this case, causing │
│ the missed fault.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep fix minimal and localized.                                 │
│  • Do not alter PMP matching/priority logic if issue is in         │
│    integration/gating.                                             │
│  • Preserve existing interfaces and timing behavior.               │
│  • Only correct the boundary-detection condition for second-half   │
│    instruction faults.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ In rtl/ibex_if_stage.sv, change the unaligned 32-bit instruction   │
│ condition from if_instr_addr[2] to if_instr_addr[1] in both places │
│ that gate +2 errors.                                               │
