To disable the I‐cache when the core is in debug mode, the fetch and cache logic needs to observe the debug signal and force cache‐bypass. This impacts at least the I‐cache itself plus the fetch and top‐level core where debug is gated. The four most critical files are:

```  
hw/core/ibex_icache.sv
hw/core/ibex_if_stage.sv
hw/core/ibex_core.sv
hw/integration/cheriot_wrapper.sv
```  

1. ibex_icache.sv – add logic to turn off caching when debug_mode is asserted.  
2. ibex_if_stage.sv – ensure fetch stage forwards debug_mode to the I‐cache and/or forces a miss.  
3. ibex_core.sv – wire up the CSR Debug bits (mstatus.MPRV, dcsr.step, haltreq, etc.) into debug_mode and export it to fetch/cache.  
4. cheriot_wrapper.sv – propagate the external debug interface through to the core’s debug_mode so that everything downstream (cache/fetch) sees it.
