The problem is clearly caused by the PMP‐address bus being declared as a fixed 32 bits on the RVFI side (in the wrapper) but only as PMP_ADDR_WIDTH bits in the CS‐register logic. To fix it, you must

  1) Change the wrapper port definition (`csr_pmpaddr_q_i`) to use PMP_ADDR_WIDTH instead of a hard-coded 32  
  2) Change the CS‐registers’ `pmp_addr_rdata` to match the RVFI width (or vice versa – make both use PMP_ADDR_WIDTH)  
  3) Ensure that the PMP_ADDR_WIDTH parameter is consistently defined (in the `cv32e40s_pkg`)  
  4) Update the RVFI package so that its pmpaddr field is sized by PMP_ADDR_WIDTH rather than 32  

Here are the four files you will almost certainly need to edit (in order of importance):

```
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/rtl/cs_registers.sv
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/rtl/cv32e40s_pkg.sv
core-v-cores/cv32e40s/rtl/rvfi_pkg.sv
```
