│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI wrapper is directly connecting PMP address CSR probes     │
│ from internal RTL signals that are not 32-bit wide when            │
│ PMP_GRANULARITY (G) > 0.                                           │
│ pmp_addr_n / pmp_addr_rdata are stored as PMP_ADDR_WIDTH = 33-G    │
│ bits, while RVFI expects 32-bit entries for csr_pmpaddr_*.         │
│                                                                    │
│ This causes:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Xcelium elaboration type mismatch (strict array element width   │
│    checking),                                                      │
│  • and incorrect RVFI CSR values if width coercion happens         │
│    implicitly (because PMP stored bits correspond to upper bits of │
│    CSR value and must be LSB-zero-extended/aligned properly).      │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, RVFI connections:                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )           │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )       │
│                                                                    │
│ These are narrow arrays connected to 32-bit RVFI ports.            │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep functional RTL storage untouched (PMP internal compact     │
│    encoding is fine).                                              │
│  • Perform explicit, deterministic conversion at the integration   │
│    boundary (wrapper).                                             │
│  • Avoid implicit width coercion on unpacked arrays.               │
│  • Preserve CSR architectural view: compact PMP address bits must  │
│    be mapped to CSR[31 : 32-PMP_ADDR_WIDTH], with low bits zero.   │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Use RVFI-side 32-bit-aligned PMP arrays in the wrapper, and        │
│ connect those to RVFI:                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  • For each region i:                                              │
│     • csr_pmpaddr_*_rvfi[i] = {pmp_addr_*[i],                      │
│       {(32-PMP_ADDR_WIDTH){1'b0}}};                                │
│  • Then connect:                                                   │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i(csr_pmpaddr_n_rvfi)                         │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i(csr_pmpaddr_q_rvfi)                         │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
