│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI interface currently expects PMP address CSR probes as     │
│ 32-bit entries per region, while the RTL stores/probes PMP         │
│ addresses with width PMP_ADDR_WIDTH = (PMP_GRANULARITY > 0) ? (33  │
│ - PMP_GRANULARITY) : 32.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ So when PMP_GRANULARITY != 0 (e.g. G=3), the wrapper connects a    │
│ [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] array into a [31:0] array port, causing       │
│ strict type mismatch in Xcelium.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, RVFI is connected with:             │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )        │
│     • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )    │
│  • In bhv/cv32e40s_rvfi.sv, csr_pmpaddr_*_i are declared as 32-bit │
│    wide arrays.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This is the exact mismatch reported by the issue.                  │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep interfaces width-consistent with producer signals.         │
│  • Parameterize widths instead of hardcoding when a core feature   │
│    (PMP granularity) changes data width.                           │
│  • Avoid relying on simulator-dependent implicit coercions for     │
│    unpacked array port connections.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Parameterize RVFI PMP address probe input width via             │
│    PMP_GRANULARITY/PMP_ADDR_WIDTH.                                 │
│  • Change csr_pmpaddr_n_i and csr_pmpaddr_q_i input declarations   │
│    in RVFI from [31:0] to [PMP_ADDR_WIDTH-1:0].                    │
│  • This removes the wrapper/RVFI type mismatch for any PMP         │
│    granularity configuration.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
