╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The RVFI probe ports for PMP address CSRs are 32-bit wide per      │
│ region, but the wrapper connects them directly to internal CSR     │
│ signals that are only PMP_ADDR_WIDTH wide (e.g. 30 bits when       │
│ PMP_GRANULARITY=3).                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ This causes:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Compile-time type mismatch (seen in Xcelium).                   │
│  • Incorrect RVFI CSR values (because raw stored PMP address       │
│    representation is not expanded to architectural CSR width).     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv, RVFI instantiation connects:           │
│                                                                    │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )           │
│  • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata )       │
│                                                                    │
│ These internal arrays are narrower than [31:0], while RVFI expects │
│ [31:0] per entry.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep architectural RVFI CSR view at full 32-bit width.          │
│  • Avoid changing functional PMP storage width in RTL datapath.    │
│  • Perform a wrapper-level adaptation (narrow internal -> 32-bit   │
│    RVFI probe).                                                    │
│  • Ensure bit placement is architecturally correct: preserved      │
│    stored bits with zero-filled dropped low bits due to            │
│    granularity.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Add RVFI adapter arrays in wrapper:                             │
│     • csr_pmpaddr_n_rvfi[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] as [31:0]                │
│     • csr_pmpaddr_q_rvfi[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] as [31:0]                │
│  • Fill them from internal narrow arrays with correct zero padding │
│    in LSBs.                                                        │
│  • Connect RVFI ports to these adapted arrays.                     │
│                                                                    │
│ This resolves both compile mismatch and wrong RVFI pmpaddr value   │
│ encoding.                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Phase 2: FIX IMPLEMENTATION                     │
