╭─ Patch Generation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem                                                         │
│     • RVFI expects PMP address CSR probe arrays as 32-bit entries: │
│        • csr_pmpaddr_n_i[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] and                      │
│          csr_pmpaddr_q_i[PMP_MAX_REGIONS] with element width       │
│          [31:0].                                                   │
│     • The wrapper currently connects these directly to RTL         │
│       internal signals (pmp_addr_n, pmp_addr_rdata) whose element  │
│       width is PMP_ADDR_WIDTH (e.g. 30 when G=3).                  │
│     • This causes:                                                 │
│        • compile-time type mismatch in Xcelium,                    │
│        • incorrect RVFI CSR values in formal (because missing low  │
│          bits are not reconstructed).                              │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│     • In bhv/cv32e40s_wrapper.sv at the RVFI instantiation,        │
│       specifically:                                                │
│        • .csr_pmpaddr_n_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_n )     │
│        • .csr_pmpaddr_q_i ( core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_rdata ) │
│  3 Best practices                                                  │
│     • Keep internal RTL storage width optimized (PMP_ADDR_WIDTH)   │
│       as-is.                                                       │
│     • Perform explicit, deterministic conversion at the monitoring │
│       boundary (wrapper/RVFI hookup).                              │
│     • Reconstruct architectural CSR width correctly (32 bits),     │
│       preserving bit placement:                                    │
│        • internal stored PMP value corresponds to upper CSR bits,  │
│          so conversion must append zeros in LSBs (<< behavior),    │
│          not MSB zero-extension.                                   │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│     • Introduce 32-bit RVFI-facing temporary arrays in wrapper.    │
│     • For each PMP region:                                         │
│        • rvfi_pmpaddr_*[i] = {core_i.cs_registers_i.pmp_addr_*[i], │
│          {(32-PMP_ADDR_WIDTH){1'b0}}};                             │
│     • Connect RVFI ports to these converted arrays.                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
