│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue reports two observable anomalies during WFI + interrupt  │
│ activity:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • A warning about reading uninitialized RAM while reading         │
│    GPIO_OUTPUT_VAL (which should be initialized/previously         │
│    written).                                                       │
│  • mip.MTIP transitions appearing at surprising points relative to │
│    instruction trace and WFI.                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ These are consistent with:                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  • Uninitialized peripheral read-data register (Dout) in GPIO APB. │
│  • Tracer CSR sampling gated by valid instead of pipeline stall    │
│    state, which can delay or mis-time visibility of asynchronous   │
│    CSR changes (like interrupt-pending bits) around WFI.           │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where the problems are in code                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/uncore/gpio_apb.sv:                                         │
│     • Dout is used to drive PRDATA but is not reset in the reset   │
│       block.                                                       │
│  • testbench/common/wallyTracer.sv:                                │
│     • CONNECT_CSR macro currently uses:                            │
│        • assign rvvi.csr[...] = valid ? val : prev...              │
│     • This freezes CSR observation whenever valid=0 (e.g. during   │
│       bubbles / WFI idle), even though comment intent is to hold   │
│       during writeback stall, not lack of retired instruction.     │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Ensure externally visible read-data paths are initialized on    │
│    reset.                                                          │
│  • For trace coherence, gate sampled architectural state using     │
│    pipeline stall/flow control, not retirement-valid alone, when   │
│    capturing asynchronous state changes.                           │
│  • Keep patch minimal and localized to avoid changing              │
│    architectural behavior.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • In gpio_apb.sv, reset Dout to zero.                             │
│  • In wallyTracer.sv, update CONNECT_CSR to hold CSR value on      │
│    StallW (as intended), not on valid.                             │
