│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ From the trace and code context, there are two likely root causes  │
│ behind the reported anomalies:                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • False “uninitialized RAM” warning on GPIO read:                 │
│    The GPIO APB peripheral’s read data flop (Dout) is not          │
│    initialized on reset. Early reads can therefore return X        │
│    transiently, which the tracer/memory checker interprets as      │
│    uninitialized data.                                             │
│  • mip.MTIP transition appears mis-timed in tracer around WFI:     │
│    In wallyTracer, CSR export via CONNECT_CSR is gated by valid    │
│    (retired instruction). This is generally correct for            │
│    instruction-retire semantics, but MIP is asynchronous           │
│    (interrupt-pending status), so gating it can make MTIP edges    │
│    appear later/oddly correlated with nearby instructions,         │
│    especially around WFI.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where in code                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/uncore/gpio_apb.sv: reset block initializes many registers  │
│    but not Dout.                                                   │
│  • testbench/common/wallyTracer.sv: CONNECT_CSR is used for MIP    │
│    (12'h344), which applies retire-time gating to an asynchronous  │
│    status CSR.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Initialize all externally-observable stateful outputs/flops on  │
│    reset (especially bus read-data flops).                         │
│  • For asynchronous interrupt-pending visibility in tracing, avoid │
│    retire-only gating for status that can change outside           │
│    instruction retirement.                                         │
│  • Keep changes minimal and targeted to avoid disrupting broader   │
│    RVVI behavior.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  4 How to fix                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • GPIO: add Dout <= '0; in reset logic.                           │
│  • Tracer: replace macro-based MIP connection with a custom        │
│    always-visible MIP mapping (ungated by valid) while preserving  │
│    change detection.                                               │
