│  • This means asynchronous CSR changes (like mip.MTIP) are hidden  │
│    until a later retiring instruction.                             │
│  • This explains delayed/misaligned interrupt-bit reporting around │
│    wfi.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ Also, wfiM is captured but not used in tracer halt signaling       │
│ (HaltM only uses DCacheFlushStart), which can further reduce       │
│ observability of wfi hold behavior.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for the fix                                      │
│                                                                    │
│  • Gate tracer pipeline-observed state with pipeline stall, not    │
│    retirement validity, when intent is “hold while WB is stalled.” │
│  • Keep behavior minimal and local to tracer (avoid changing       │
│    core/peripheral behavior unless clearly needed).                │
│  • Preserve existing interfaces and signal naming.                 │
│                                                                    │
