│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has two concurrent stimulus sources:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • deterministic AXI write/read sanity check                       │
│    (proc_generate_axi_traffic)                                     │
│  • randomized direct register load toggling                        │
│    (proc_generate_direct_load via toggle_load)                     │
│                                                                    │
│ In some seeds, random reg_load activity starts early and           │
│ overwrites register bytes before/around the deterministic          │
│ readback. That causes nondeterministic mismatch like:              │
│                                                                    │
│  • expected: 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF                                  │
│  • got: value with random-byte corruption (example log shows       │
│    de01beef fragment)                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load spawns toggle_load immediately.       │
│  • toggle_load begins random load loop right after reset.          │
│  • deterministic check in proc_generate_axi_traffic assumes        │
│    register content remains what was written, but can be clobbered │
│    by random loads.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic sanity checks isolated from                  │
│    random/background traffic.                                      │
│  • Avoid timing/seed-dependent races between independent test      │
│    processes.                                                      │
│  • Use explicit synchronization instead of relying on random wait  │
│    ranges.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce an explicit synchronization event:                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • Declare a module-scope event (start_rand_load).                 │
│  • Trigger it in proc_generate_axi_traffic after deterministic     │
│    write/read assertions pass.                                     │
│  • Make each toggle_load task wait for this event before entering  │
│    its forever random loop.                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ This is minimal, robust, and preserves existing random test        │
│ behavior after the deterministic phase.                            │
