│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs is flaky for some seeds because the background    │
│ rand_load generator (toggle_load) can start modifying register     │
│ bytes before the directed sanity check completes (the write/read   │
│ of address 0x0 expecting DEADBEEF...).                             │
│ So the deterministic read assertion occasionally sees modified     │
│ data (e.g. de01beef) and fails.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv, inside:                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • initial begin : proc_generate_direct_load ... toggle_load(j);   │
│  • task automatic toggle_load(int unsigned byte_i);                │
│                                                                    │
│ toggle_load starts right after reset and immediately enters random │
│ load activity. This can overlap with the known-value write/read    │
│ check in proc_generate_axi_traffic.                                │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed checks deterministic and isolated from randomized │
│    background traffic.                                             │
│  • Synchronize concurrent testbench threads with protocol          │
│    events/signals, not seed-dependent timing.                      │
│  • Avoid magic delays where possible.                              │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Delay start of random reg_load activity until after the first      │
│ AXI-Lite read response handshake is observed (master.r_valid &&    │
│ master.r_ready), which corresponds to the directed read check      │
│ completion in this TB flow.                                        │
│ This preserves random-load behavior for the randomized phase while │
│ preventing collision with the deterministic assertion.             │
