│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The failure is caused by a race between deterministic sanity       │
│ checks and randomized direct register loads in                     │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs.sv.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • The test writes DEADBEEFDEADBEEF to address 0x0, then           │
│    immediately reads it back and expects the same value.           │
│  • In parallel, proc_generate_direct_load starts right after reset │
│    and can randomly assert reg_load[...], which overwrites         │
│    register bytes.                                                 │
│  • Depending on seed/timing, a random load can occur between the   │
│    write and read, producing mismatched readback data and          │
│    assertion failure.                                              │
│                                                                    │
