│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a race between:                               │
│                                                                    │
│  • the directed sanity check (write known value, read it back,     │
│    assert exact match), and                                        │
│  • the random reg_load stimulus generated by toggle_load().        │
│                                                                    │
│ For some seeds, random load updates the same register bytes        │
│ before/during the directed readback, so the read data is no longer │
│ 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF (example got de01beef), causing               │
│ non-deterministic assertion failures.                              │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() threads          │
│    immediately.                                                    │
│  • toggle_load() starts random load activity shortly after reset   │
│    and runs forever.                                               │
│  • Meanwhile, proc_generate_axi_traffic performs the directed      │
│    write/read check assuming register content is stable.           │
│                                                                    │
│ So the collision is between:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic (directed check), and                 │
│  • toggle_load() (random load pulses on reg_load/reg_d).           │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed smoke checks deterministic.                       │
│  • Start random background stimuli only after deterministic checks │
│    complete.                                                       │
│  • Make minimal changes; preserve existing random behavior for the │
│    rest of the test.                                               │
│  • Avoid timing hacks; use explicit synchronization (enable        │
│    flag/event).                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a synchronization flag (e.g. rand_load_enable):          │
│                                                                    │
│  • initialize it to 0,                                             │
│  • set it to 1 only after directed write/read assertions complete, │
│  • in each toggle_load() task, wait for this flag before entering  │
│    random forever loop.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ This prevents random load from corrupting the known-value readback │
│ while keeping existing random stress after that point.             │
