│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a seed-dependent failure because random       │
│ direct register loads (reg_load/reg_d) can start too early and     │
│ overwrite bytes of the register before the directed write/read     │
│ sanity check completes.                                            │
│ So instead of reading back 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF, the test          │
│ occasionally reads a partially overwritten value like de01beef.    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts spawning toggle_load() threads │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load() then randomly asserts reg_load and writes random  │
│    bytes forever.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ This can race with the directed write/read in                      │
│ proc_generate_axi_traffic.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep directed sanity checks deterministic.                      │
│  • Start randomized background stimulus only after directed checks │
│    are done (or after a clear synchronization point).              │
│  • Avoid fragile reset-edge assumptions inside reusable tasks; use │
│    wait(rst_n) so task works whether reset already happened or     │
│    not.                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  • Delay starting proc_generate_direct_load threads until after    │
│    the first read response handshake (master.r_valid &&            │
│    master.r_ready), which corresponds to the directed readback     │
│    phase.                                                          │
│  • Change toggle_load reset wait from @(posedge rst_n) to          │
│    wait(rst_n) so it does not deadlock when started after reset is │
│    already high.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
