│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a startup race: the random direct-load        │
│ stimulus (toggle_load) can begin modifying register bytes before   │
│ the test’s deterministic “write known value, then read back same   │
│ value” check completes.                                            │
│ So in some seeds, a byte gets overwritten between the write and    │
│ read, causing failures like:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • expected: 64'hDEADBEEFDEADBEEF                                  │
│  • observed: partially modified value (e.g. ...DE01BEEF...)        │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it happens                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is in test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv, block:                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs deterministic write/read and │
│    asserts fixed readback.                                         │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load() threads          │
│    immediately after reset, which can collide with that            │
│    deterministic readback.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic checks isolated from randomized background   │
│    traffic.                                                        │
│  • Synchronize concurrent testbench processes explicitly instead   │
│    of relying on timing luck.                                      │
│  • Make minimal changes that preserve existing random-load         │
│    behavior after the deterministic sanity check.                  │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Delay starting proc_generate_direct_load until after the first AXI │
│ read response handshake is observed.                               │
│ In this testbench flow, that first read response corresponds to    │
│ the deterministic known-register readback. After that, random      │
│ direct-load threads can safely start.                              │
