│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Problem summary                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ tb_axi_lite_regs has a nondeterministic failure: the “known        │
│ register” readback check sometimes gets corrupted data (de01beef   │
│ instead of deadbeefdeadbeef) for specific seeds.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ This happens because randomized direct-load traffic (toggle_load)  │
│ can update register bytes while the deterministic write/read       │
│ sanity check is running.                                           │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Where it occurs                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ In test/tb_axi_lite_regs.sv:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  • proc_generate_axi_traffic performs a deterministic write/read   │
│    sequence first.                                                 │
│  • proc_generate_direct_load starts toggle_load workers            │
│    immediately after reset.                                        │
│  • toggle_load continuously asserts reg_load with random byte      │
│    values.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ So there is a race/collision between the deterministic check and   │
│ random load injection.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Best practices for fix                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep deterministic sanity checks isolated from random           │
│    background stimulus.                                            │
│  • Gate background random generators until directed checks         │
│    complete.                                                       │
│  • Make minimal changes to preserve existing random testing        │
│    behavior afterward.                                             │
│                                                                    │
│  4 Fix approach                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Introduce a small synchronization flag:                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • Initialize it to 0.                                             │
│  • Set it to 1 only after the deterministic write/read check is    │
│    done.                                                           │
│  • In toggle_load, wait for this flag before entering the random   │
│    load loop.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ This removes seed-dependent collisions during the known-value      │
│ check, while preserving random load behavior for the rest of       │
│ simulation.                                                        │
