I focused on where the four AXI port instances named s_data_master, s_data_slave, s_data_in_bus and s_data_out_bus are actually hooked up – the RTL that wires the cluster’s data ports into the SoC AXI fabric.  In pulp_soc_pr23 they live in:

– the cluster‐side wrapper that bridges the cluster’s data MEM ports into AXI (where s_data_master and s_data_slave get instantiated)  
– the top‐level SoC fabric file where the two AXI_BUS ports for data in/out get instantiated  

All of those sit under `hw/SoC/…`, and the AXI_BUS/AXI_BUS_ASYNC definitions they instantiate live under `hw/common/axi`.  Those four files will need to have their `.AXI_ID_WIDTH` parameters corrected from the blanket `AXI_ID_OUT_WIDTH` to the proper `AXI_ID_IN_WIDTH` or `AXI_ID_OUT_WIDTH` on each port:

``` 
hw/SoC/cluster2axi.sv
hw/SoC/pulp_soc.sv
hw/common/axi/AXI_BUS_ASYNC.sv
hw/common/axi/AXI_BUS.sv
```
