│                                                                    │
│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1) What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that dmi_jtag_tap.sv generates trst_no using logic    │
│ that is clocked by tck_i and depends on a combinational signal     │
│ (trst_sync1) derived from TAP state logic. This makes trst_no      │
│ prone to glitches and incorrect transient values. Since trst_no is │
│ used as an asynchronous reset in dmi_jtag.sv and dmi_cdc.sv, a     │
│ glitch can unintentionally reset those modules.                    │
│                                                                    │
│ In short:                                                          │
│                                                                    │
│  • The intent is to reset the JTAG/DMI logic by cycling TMS into   │
│    TestLogicReset.                                                 │
│  • The implementation of the generated reset is unsafe.            │
│  • trst_no should not be derived in a way that can glitch or       │
│    behave asynchronously from combinational state changes.         │
│                                                                    │
│                    2) Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problematic code is in:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • src/dmi_jtag_tap.sv                                             │
│                                                                    │
│ Specifically the block:                                            │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  logic trst_sync1, trst_sync2;                                     │
│                                                                    │
│  always_ff @(posedge tck_i or negedge trst_ni) begin               │
│    if (!trst_ni) begin                                             │
│      trst_sync2 <= 1'b0;                                           │
│    end else begin                                                  │
│      trst_sync2 <= trst_sync1;                                     │
│      trst_no    <= trst_sync2;                                     │
│    end                                                             │
│  end                                                               │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ and its dependency here:                                           │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  always_comb begin : p_tap_fsm                                     │
│    trst_sync1         = trst_ni;                                   │
│    ...                                                             │
│    TestLogicReset: begin                                           │
│      ...                                                           │
│      trst_sync1 = 1'b1;                                            │
│    end                                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ The combination of:                                                │
│                                                                    │
│  • trst_sync1 being assigned in combinational logic,               │
│  • trst_no being driven from a sequential block but not cleanly    │
│    synchronized,                                                   │
│  • and trst_no effectively acting like an asynchronous reset,      │
│                                                                    │
│ is what makes the design unsafe.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│               3) Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix should follow these principles:                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • Do not generate asynchronous reset-like signals from            │
│    combinational state transitions unless absolutely necessary and │
│    fully synchronized.                                             │
│  • Avoid glitch-prone reset generation from mixed                  │
│    combinational/sequential logic.                                 │
│  • Use a clean, registered reset signal if the goal is to reset    │
│    based on TAP state.                                             │
│  • Keep reset generation synchronous to the relevant clock (tck_i) │
│    to ensure stable behavior.                                      │
│  • Minimize changes and preserve intended functionality.           │
│                                                                    │
│                     4) How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The safest fix is to remove the unsafe generated-reset behavior    │
│ and instead keep trst_no directly tied to the external reset       │
│ (trst_ni) or implement a fully synchronous reset scheme.           │
│                                                                    │
│ Given the issue description and the minimal-change requirement,    │
│ the best fix is:                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • Remove the logic that tries to create trst_no by cycling        │
│    through TestLogicReset.                                         │
│  • Keep trst_no stable and non-glitchy by assigning it directly    │
│    from trst_ni or otherwise ensuring it is only updated           │
│    synchronously in a safe way.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This avoids unintended asynchronous resets in downstream modules.  │
│                                                                    │
