│                       Phase 1: FIX ANALYSIS                        │
│                                                                    │
│                       1. What the problem is                       │
│                                                                    │
│ The FPGA build of Occamy fails during synthesis because            │
│ occamy_xilinx.sv includes a missing header file:                   │
│                                                                    │
│  • axi_flat.svh is not present in the repository                   │
│  • As a result, the macros AXI_FLATTEN_MASTER and                  │
│    AXI_FLATTEN_SLAVE are undefined                                 │
│  • This breaks synthesis when building occamy_vcu128               │
│                                                                    │
│                    2. Where the problem occurs                     │
│                                                                    │
│ The problem is in hw/system/occamy/src/occamy_xilinx.sv:           │
│                                                                    │
│  • At the top of the file, it has:                                 │
│     • `include "axi_flat.svh"                                      │
│  • Later in the same file, it uses:                                │
│     • `AXI_FLATTEN_MASTER(...)                                     │
│     • `AXI_FLATTEN_SLAVE(...)                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Because the included file is missing, these macros are not         │
│ defined.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│               3. Best practices to take into account               │
│                                                                    │
│  • Keep the fix minimal and focused                                │
│  • Preserve existing generated/system integration code structure   │
│  • Avoid changing unrelated AXI wiring logic                       │
│  • Prefer restoring missing generated helper functionality rather  │
│    than rewriting interface code                                   │
│  • Ensure the fix is synthesis-friendly and compatible with        │
│    existing macros used by the design                              │
│                                                                    │
│                     4. How to fix the problem                      │
│                                                                    │
│ The correct fix is to restore the missing header file axi_flat.svh │
│ in the repository, since occamy_xilinx.sv depends on it for AXI    │
│ flattening macros.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is not in the use sites themselves; they are correct     │
│ assuming the helper header exists. Therefore, the minimal fix is   │
│ to add the missing include file containing definitions for:        │
